WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.583
(spooky music)

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:06.993
- Are you scared Jason?

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:11.530
(suspenseful music)

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.497
- Now brace yourself,
the apartment's small,

00:00:13.497 --> 00:00:14.677
a pied-a-terre, but,

00:00:14.677 --> 00:00:16.670
[Hermione And Veronica In
Unison] Quality always.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:18.510
- Are you excited?

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:19.763
Nervous?

00:00:19.763 --> 00:00:22.350
- Both. (laughs)

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.640
I haven't seen him all summer.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.120
- [Archie Andrews] So,
what was the highlight?

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:27.610
- Of my internship?

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:30.743
The Toni Morrison book release
party I organized, by far.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.500
- Uh, can I sit, Jughead?

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.051
- If you want.

00:00:37.051 --> 00:00:38.390
- If he is dead, Hal...

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:42.163
I hope in those last moments he suffered.

00:00:43.299 --> 00:00:45.633
May Jason Blossom burn in hell.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.720
- Hey, you stopping by the site later?

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:51.150
- Dad, it's my first day.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.271
- [Josie Singing] Lost in the moment

00:00:52.271 --> 00:00:53.525
dancing in cages.

00:00:53.525 --> 00:00:54.358
- Ooh-ooh.

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:57.479
- Mm.

00:00:57.479 --> 00:00:58.460
Excuse me.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.210
This is a closed rehearsal.

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:03.620
- Bro, you are ready for football.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:04.453
I'm not kidding, dude,

00:01:04.453 --> 00:01:05.449
you got ripped.

00:01:05.449 --> 00:01:08.920
(suspenseful music)

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.660
- Where's the rest of it?

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:12.490
- How are you holding up?

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:13.670
- How do you think?

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:15.940
- Would you like to give
me a quote regarding--

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:16.773
- Alice--

00:01:16.773 --> 00:01:18.020
- All right, sweetheart.
- Cooper.

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:21.500
- For the record,

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:22.960
I'm not gay.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:23.793
- Hey, honey.

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:26.378
Just wanted you to know
it's gonna be a bit of a

00:01:26.378 --> 00:01:27.606
late night for us.

00:01:27.606 --> 00:01:28.439
(upbeat music)

00:01:28.439 --> 00:01:29.272
- Miss Grundy?

00:01:29.272 --> 00:01:30.105
Hey.

00:01:30.105 --> 00:01:31.227
- Archie.

00:01:31.227 --> 00:01:34.060
What are you doing walking in this heat?

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.690
- Hey, Pop,

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:37.470
Betty hasn't come in tonight has she?

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:40.543
- No, just the night hawks in tonight.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.212
- Go, get around them, get around them.

00:01:43.212 --> 00:01:44.780
(whistle blowing in distance)

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:46.300
Let's move.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:47.133
Andrews.

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:49.630
(whistle blowing in distance)

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:52.150
- Good morning students, this
is your principal speaking.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:55.070
There have been many inquiries
about the upcoming pep rally,

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:56.930
so let me state clearly,

00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:58.703
it is happening as scheduled.

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:03.920
- Most of you already know the details,

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.930
but your classmate Jason
Blossom's body was found

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:08.163
late Saturday night.

00:02:08.163 --> 00:02:08.996
(applause)

00:02:08.996 --> 00:02:10.693
- Thank you, Principal Weatherbee.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:14.960
It is heartening to see
so many of you here,

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:16.857
even in weather like this.

00:02:16.857 --> 00:02:17.910
- [Chuck Clayton] Let me try again.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:18.743
- [Veronica Lodge] Let me see it.

00:02:18.743 --> 00:02:19.576
- [Chuck Clayton] You don't trust me?

00:02:19.576 --> 00:02:21.260
- No, no, no, fine you can take it.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:22.310
Okay, let me see.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:23.143
Photo approval.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:27.680
- I started asking around to
see if what happened to you

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:28.880
happened to anyone else,

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.040
if anyone would go on record.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:32.440
- I will.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:33.510
100 percent.

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:36.323
- And in that moment of
hesitation, you're dead.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:39.913
All of you are dead.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:43.379
- At ease, Doiley.

00:02:43.379 --> 00:02:46.129
(dramatic music)

00:02:47.048 --> 00:02:47.881
- Okay, okay.

00:02:48.804 --> 00:02:50.478
- I'm Joaquin by the way.

00:02:50.478 --> 00:02:52.379
(peaceful music)

00:02:52.379 --> 00:02:53.212
- Betty.

00:02:53.212 --> 00:02:56.018
(joyful laughter)

00:02:56.018 --> 00:02:57.304
(upbeat music)

00:02:57.304 --> 00:02:58.137
- Mom?

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:00.312
- Hi, honey.

00:03:00.312 --> 00:03:02.307
(upbeat music)

00:03:02.307 --> 00:03:03.720
- Give me your wallet!

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:06.688
(suspenseful music)

00:03:06.688 --> 00:03:07.761
(gun bangs)

00:03:07.761 --> 00:03:11.035
♪ My God ♪

00:03:11.035 --> 00:03:12.800
♪ My God ♪

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.700
- I came home earlier to surprise you.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.233
- Midge Klump.

00:03:20.247 --> 00:03:21.950
The Klumpster.

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:22.783
- Reggie.

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:25.480
What do you know about jingle-jangle?

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:29.830
- Forsythe Pendleton Jones The Third.

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:31.770
(camera shutter sound)

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.543
- Topaz, let's bounce.

00:03:34.804 --> 00:03:37.280
He told me he wants to
earn his serpent stripes,

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:38.950
I say bring us the head
of that North sider

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:39.783
and you're in.

00:03:39.783 --> 00:03:40.904
- I'm down with that.

00:03:40.904 --> 00:03:42.660
(Sweet Pea laughs and bangs on table)

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:43.493
- We're...

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.113
- I know who you are.

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:48.970
The sisters gave me your address

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:50.120
when I turned eighteen.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:53.580
- Jughead?

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:54.413
- Jellybean?

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:57.880
- Thought I smelled something rotten.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:58.713
- Jughead?

00:04:00.214 --> 00:04:01.053
- Hey, mom.

00:04:02.477 --> 00:04:04.360
- Listen, bro, since
we're gonna be cellmates--

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.203
- Nice shoes.

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:08.063
I'd keep 'em tied real tight.

00:04:10.247 --> 00:04:12.700
- Hi, I'm Everlyn, and you're...

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:13.783
Betty Cooper?

00:04:15.691 --> 00:04:17.590
- It's nice to meet you, Cheryl.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.423
- Can I help you?

00:04:18.423 --> 00:04:20.060
- Mr Jones?

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:21.640
I'm Agent Smith with the FBI.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:23.390
Is Betty Cooper here by any chance?

